      "message": "As part of the arm64 Linux kernel loader change (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/crosvm/crosvm/+/3976062), I am planning on changing `AARCH64_KERNEL_OFFSET` to 0, effectively loading the kernel (whether it\u0027s an ARM64 Linux image or an ELF) at the very beginning of guest memory.\n\nOnce AARCH64_KERNEL_OFFSET is 0, does this patch affect the final load address? I think it should be equivalent to what this patch is trying to accomplish without changing the ELF code, although I don\u0027t have a setup to verify this locally.",
